From 3fe0a2bb3455ff9e8fb0810ab6b8748e1b09d848 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zach Denton <z@chdenton.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 20:01:33 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] amdgpu: v_permlanex16 cross-lane recipe and an f32 -> f16
 rhs fragment repack in registers

xor-16 subgroup shuffles on wave32 gfx11 lower to v_permlanex16_b32 (SGPR selectors
0x76543210 / 0xfedcba98) instead of ds_swizzle. A new fragment repack strategy,
result_f32_to_rhs_b16_permlane, turns an f32 WMMA result (or accumulator) fragment into
an f16 rhs fragment without an LDS round trip: exchange each f32 with lane ^ 16, convert
both halves, v_pack_b32_f16, then a v_perm_b32 selected per lane half. Verified exact
against O = V . f16(A . B^T) on gfx1151; existing kernels' code is unchanged.
